{"title":"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The volume of an orthogonal <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parallelepiped\" title=\"Parallelepiped\">parallelepiped</a> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/b/7eb004fcb69934b55871d419e8e4a396b46ad569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$132\\;\\mathrm{cm}^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" /> and its dimensions are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integers</a>. The minimum sum of the dimensions is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/9/ba927dc72df4fb96c6b1fbf0cce5f5a7bddd1ce1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } 27\\;\\mathrm{ cm}\\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } 19\\;\\mathrm{ cm}\\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ }20\\;\\mathrm{ cm}\\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } 18\\;\\mathrm{ cm}\\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } \\mathrm{None\\ of\\ these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"591\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/89767dd34aa1facf59517962dcac066c378f5b77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle V = lwh$\" width=\"68\" height=\"12\" />, so we want to minimize the sum of three integers whose product is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc47aee7abcc370f258e3df2aa872d29bf084960.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle 132 = 2^2\\cdot3\\cdot11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"120\" height=\"15\" />. To do this, the factors must be as close together as possible. Therefore, none of the factors will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and one will likely be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. This implies that the factors are minimized when they are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/2/b22083463426b008b13e0f6a721e51c9a51beeaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,\\ 4,\\ 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" />, and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311f77e4fd838a22d5079f9555b8638b447196ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 4 + 11 = 18 \\Longrightarrow \\mathrm{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"175\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; align:center; width:60%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum\">2007 Cyprus MO, Lyceum</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problems\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" al